      <h2 class="profile-section-title" id="timeline-title">Timeline</h2>
      <ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">1789</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-the-united-states">Constitution of the United States</a> takes effect and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a> is inaugurated as the first president</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1803</span><span class="rf-text">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marbury-v-madison">Marbury v. Madison</a> the Supreme Court asserts its power to strike down acts of Congress</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1824</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>’s first federal constitution creates a presidency on the American model</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1889</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>’s monarchy falls and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deodoro-da-fonseca">Deodoro da Fonseca</a> becomes the first president of a presidential republic</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1951</span><span class="rf-text">The Twenty-second Amendment limits American presidents to two terms</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1973</span><span class="rf-text">Chile’s armed forces overthrow President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador-allende">Salvador Allende</a>, ending four decades of constitutional rule</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1974</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-nixon">Richard Nixon</a> resigns as Congress moves to impeach him over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/watergate-scandal">Watergate scandal</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1987</span><span class="rf-text">After mass protests, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a> adopts a constitution with direct presidential elections</span></li></ol>
